            0.42,
            0.065
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 8 | Part-II"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 1,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.087,
            0.581,
            0.151
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "？ How do we find the area of a parallelogram by dissecting it into a rectangle? We have"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 2,
          "bbox": [
            0.152,
            0.154,
            0.641,
            0.194
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Area of the parallelogram ABCD = Area of the rectangle ABYX."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 3,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.197,
            0.57,
            0.243
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Area of the rectangle ABYX = AX × XY. AX is the height of the parallelogram."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.658,
            0.093,
            0.898,
            0.216
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 4,
              "bbox": [
                0.658,
                0.093,
                0.898,
                0.216
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_14_image_4.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.111,
            0.253,
            0.536,
            0.277
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Is there a relation between XY and DC?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.279,
            0.848,
            0.319
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Since DX = CY, we get DC = XY by adding the common part XC to DX and CY. Since DC is the base of the parallelogram, we get"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.296,
            0.332,
            0.7,
            0.353
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Area of the parallelogram = base × height."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 8,
          "bbox": [
            0.11,
            0.4,
            0.518,
            0.479
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Can the area of the parallelogram be determined by taking another side as the base and its corresponding height?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "index": 9,
          "bbox": [
            0.529,
            0.378,
            0.847,
            0.499
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "image_body",
              "index": 9,
              "bbox": [
                0.529,
                0.378,
                0.847,
                0.499
              ],
              "image_path": "images/page_14_image_9.jpg",
              "content": ""
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 10,
          "bbox": [
            0.109,
            0.508,
            0.846,
            0.549
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "? Can the parallelogram be cut along CZ and rearranged to form a rectangle?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 11,
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.551,
            0.847,
            0.591
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "It can be seen that this is indeed possible, and so any side and its corresponding height can be used to find the area of a parallelogram."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "index": 12,
          "bbox": [
            0.113,
            0.6,
            0.295,
            0.622
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Figure it Out"
            }
          ],
          "level": 2
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 13,
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.625,
            0.653,
            0.646
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "1. Observe the parallelograms in the figure below."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 14,
          "bbox": [
            0.199,
            0.655,
            0.828,
            0.676
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(i) What can we say about the areas of all these parallelograms?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 15,
          "bbox": [
            0.196,
            0.679,
            0.847,
            0.736
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "(ii) What can we say about their perimeters? Which figure appears to have the maximum perimeter, and which has the minimum perimeter?"
            }
          ]
        },
